In all these folders there should be a "Compile_Exec.txt" which
tells you exactly the settings used to produce each supercell_corr2.dat file.
This file is then converted into a lammps data.lammps file (These have been removed),
and then this is relaxed using lammps and the final relaxed positions are contained
in the files "positions.dat"


We are going to have these 5, 10, 15, 25 % InGaN wells, the 15% with and without wwfs
and of different heights, all contained together in one github repo. The github repo
will show how to reproduce any of the configurations (which we can do test runs of)
and how to do the subsequent electronic structure calculations. We can then delete
all the mess that is left behind.


- The 5% is a fresh 5% that was made for the green gap paper. This and also the folders
  whiwh are just numbers can be easily reproduced and you can start with these for the 
  green-gap paper.

- For the other In contents however, they started with the RSC paper,
  and were then added to in subsequent papers. This makes the issue very
  messy, and what we should actually do is just show how their averages could be 
  reproduced statistically. If This is not possible, then they are not worth
  reproducing or keeping.

- As you will not be reproducing all the data, you can have a folder for each paper.
